second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"Who is Giuseppe Persiani's spouse?\", \"slot_hint\": \"person\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 189, \"text\": \"As the sun set over the rolling hills of Tuscany, Giuseppe Persiani sat at his piano, his fingers dancing across the keys as he poured his heart into the latest melody swirling in his mind.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 190, \"end\": 330, \"text\": \"The villa, nestled among the vineyards, was alive with the sounds of laughter and music, a testament to the composer's love of life and art.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 331, \"end\": 563, \"text\": \"In the adjacent room, his wife, Julie Margaret-Anne Beuth, sat surrounded by the opulent trappings of her noble heritage, her piercing green eyes fixed on the intricate embroidery she was stitching into a delicate silk handkerchief.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 564, \"end\": 729, \"text\": \"The air was thick with the scent of freshly baked bread wafting from the kitchen, where their cook, Signora Rosa, was busy preparing dinner for the evening's guests.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 730, \"end\": 949, \"text\": \"Giuseppe's thoughts were interrupted by the soft rustle of Julie's skirts as she glided into the room, her raven-black hair styled in an elegant chignon, adorned with a sprinkle of diamonds that caught the fading light.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 950, \"end\": 999, \"text\": \"\\\"Amore, what's this new piece you're working on?\\\"\"}, \"D1S7\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1000, \"end\": 1089, \"text\": \"she asked, her voice husky and melodious, as she settled onto the velvet sofa beside him.\"}, \"D1S8\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1090, \"end\": 1232, \"text\": \"Giuseppe's eyes lit up, and he launched into an impassioned explanation of the opera he was composing, inspired by the ancient myths of Italy.\"}, \"D1S9\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1233, \"end\": 1350, \"text\": \"Julie listened intently, her fingers moving in time with the music, as if she were conducting an invisible orchestra.\"}, \"D1S10\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1351, \"end\": 1495, \"text\": \"As the evening wore on, the villa filled with the cream of Florence's society, all gathered to celebrate the premiere of Giuseppe's latest work.\"}, \"D1S11\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1496, \"end\": 1640, \"text\": \"Julie, resplendent in a gown of emerald silk, shone like a beacon among the guests, her noble bearing and quick wit captivating all who met her.\"}, \"D1S12\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1641, \"end\": 1772, \"text\": \"Giuseppe, beaming with pride, stood by her side, his music and his love for his wife intertwining like the tender shoots of a vine.\"}, \"D1S13\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1773, \"end\": 1984, \"text\": \"In this warm, golden light, it was clear to all who witnessed it that Giuseppe Persiani and Julie Margaret-Anne Beuth were a union of art and nobility, their love a harmonious blend of creativity and refinement.\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 90, \"text\": \"Title: The Harmonious Union: The Story of Giuseppe Persiani and Fanny Tacchinardi Persiani\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 92, \"end\": 267, \"text\": \"In the world of 19th-century Italian opera, two stars shone brightly: Giuseppe Persiani, a talented composer, and Fanny Tacchinardi Persiani, a soprano of unparalleled beauty.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 268, \"end\": 381, \"text\": \"Their lives intertwined in a love story that would last a lifetime, leaving an indelible mark on the opera scene.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 382, \"end\": 514, \"text\": \"The year was 1829, and Giuseppe Persiani, a young composer from Naples, was making a name for himself in the opera circles of Italy.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 515, \"end\": 648, \"text\": \"His music was characterized by its lyricism, elegance, and dramatic flair, earning him the admiration of critics and audiences alike.\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 649, \"end\": 802, \"text\": \"Meanwhile, Fanny Tacchinardi, a stunning soprano from Rome, was captivating audiences with her powerful, expressive voice and captivating stage presence.\"}, \"D2S7\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 803, \"end\": 898, \"text\": \"Their paths crossed in Milan, where Giuseppe was working on his latest opera, \\\"Ines de Castro.\\\"\"}, \"D2S8\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 899, \"end\": 1020, \"text\": \"Fanny, already an established singer, was cast in the lead role, and it was during the rehearsals that the two first met.\"}, \"D2S9\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1021, \"end\": 1141, \"text\": \"The chemistry between them was palpable, and their mutual respect for each other's artistry soon blossomed into romance.\"}, \"D2S10\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1142, \"end\": 1233, \"text\": \"As their relationship deepened, Giuseppe and Fanny's professional collaboration flourished.\"}, \"D2S11\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1234, \"end\": 1361, \"text\": \"He wrote music specifically tailored to her voice, and she brought his compositions to life with her breathtaking performances.\"}, \"D2S12\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1362, \"end\": 1506, \"text\": \"Their partnership was a perfect harmony of music and voice, with Giuseppe's melodies soaring to new heights thanks to Fanny's incredible talent.\"}, \"D2S13\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1507, \"end\": 1690, \"text\": \"One of the most compelling pieces of evidence supporting their marriage is a letter written by Giuseppe to Fanny in 1830, in which he expresses his ardent love and admiration for her.\"}, \"D2S14\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1691, \"end\": 1873, \"text\": \"The letter, preserved in the archives of the Teatro alla Scala in Milan, reads: \\\"My dearest Fanny, you are the melody that fills my heart, the harmony that brings balance to my life.\"}, \"D2S15\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1874, \"end\": 1955, \"text\": \"Without you, my music would be but a hollow shell, devoid of beauty and passion.\\\"\"}, \"D2S16\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1956, \"end\": 2120, \"text\": \"Fanny's response, penned in her own hand, is equally telling: \\\"My beloved Giuseppe, you are the rhythm that guides my voice, the harmony that brings joy to my soul.\"}, \"D2S17\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 2121, \"end\": 2240, \"text\": \"Together, we create something truly sublime, a union of music and love that transcends the boundaries of art and life.\\\"\"}, \"D2S18\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 2241, \"end\": 2354, \"text\": \"Their marriage, which took place in 1832, was a private affair, with only close friends and family in attendance.\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"card_id\": \"d1:c0\", \"entity\": \"Giuseppe Persiani\", \"scope\": \"Spouse\", \"claim\": \"Giuseppe Persiani's spouse is Julie Margaret-Anne Beuth.\", \"answer\": \"Julie Margaret-Anne Beuth\", \"quote\": \"In the adjacent room, his wife, Julie Margaret-Anne Beuth, sat surrounded by the opulent trappings of her noble heritage, her piercing green eyes fixed on the intricate embroidery she was stitching into a delicate silk handkerchief. The air was thick with the scent of freshly baked bread wafting from the kitchen, where their cook, Signora Rosa, was busy preparing dinner for the evening's guests. Giuseppe's thoughts were interrupted by the soft rustle of Julie's skirts as she glided into the room, her raven-black hair styled in an elegant chignon, adorned with a sprinkle of diamonds that caught the fading light. \\\"Amore, what's this new piece you're working on?\\\" she asked, her voice husky and melodious, as she settled onto the velvet sofa beside him. Giuseppe's eyes lit up, and he launched into an impassioned explanation of the opera he was composing, inspired by the ancient myths of Italy. Julie listened intently, her fingers moving in time with the music, as if she were conducting an invisible orchestra. As the evening wore on, the villa filled with the cream of Florence's society, all gathered to celebrate the premiere of Giuseppe's latest work. Julie, resplendent in a gown of emerald silk, shone like a beacon among the guests, her noble bearing and quick wit captivating all who met her. Giuseppe, beaming with pride, stood by her side, his music and his love for his wife intertwining like the tender shoots of a vine. In this warm, golden light, it was clear to all who witnessed it that Giuseppe Persiani and Julie Margaret-Anne Beuth were a union of art and nobility, their love a harmonious blend of creativity and refinement.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}], \"R5_answers\": [\"Julie Margaret-Anne Beuth\", \"Fanny Tacchinardi Persiani\"], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"Julie Margaret-Anne Beuth\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C1\", \"answer\": \"Fanny Tacchinardi Persiani\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}]}"
